// Tool descriptions
description.agent-call: Runs another AI agent with a custom instruction, user message and a set of allowed tools and skills.
description.agent-describe_image: Describes the content of an image using a separate vision-capable AI agent.
description.clipboard-copy: Copies a piece of text to the system clipboard.
description.clipboard-read: Reads the current text content of the system clipboard.
description.csx-execute: Runs C# code with access to .NET APIs and returns the script result.
description.db-execute: Executes a SQL statement against the active database and returns the result.
description.db-list: Lists the database connections configured in the chat and highlights the currently active one.
description.db-schema: Shows the schema of the active database: tables, views and their columns.
description.db-switch: Activates a database connection for the current chat session by name or a custom connection string.
description.execute-python: Runs Python code in an isolated virtual environment and shows live output in a terminal.
description.execute-python_venv_shell: Runs a shell command inside the Python virtual environment, for example to install packages with pip.
description.forms-choice: Lets the user pick one or more options from a list, optionally allowing a custom answer.
description.forms-confirm: Asks the user to confirm an action with confirm and cancel buttons.
description.forms-file_picker: Opens a file dialog so the user can select a file, folder or save location.
description.forms-input: Requests structured data from the user through a form with one or more fields.
description.fs-apply_diff: Edits a text file by deleting a range of lines and inserting new text at a specified line.
description.fs-copy_directory: Copies a directory and all of its contents to a new location.
description.fs-copy_file: Copies a file to a new location, replacing the destination file if needed.
description.fs-create_directory: Creates a new directory at the specified path.
description.fs-delete_directory: Deletes a directory together with all of its contents.
description.fs-delete_file: Deletes a specified file from the working directory.
description.fs-edit: Finds a text fragment or a regular expression in a file and replaces, inserts, or deletes the matched content.
description.fs-get_file_info: Returns file metadata: name, type, size, creation and modification dates, and attributes.
description.fs-glob: Finds files and directories that match a glob pattern in the specified folder.
description.fs-grep: Searches files for lines matching a regular expression pattern.
description.fs-move_directory: Moves a directory and all of its contents to a new location.
description.fs-open_file: Opens a file with its default application on the system.
description.fs-open_in_explorer: Opens a file or directory in the system file explorer, highlighting the file if it exists.
description.fs-read_binary_file: Reads a binary file as a hex dump within the specified byte range.
description.fs-read_document_file: Extracts text from documents (PDF, DOCX, PPTX) page by page.
description.fs-read_entry: Reads a file line by line or lists the contents of a directory at the given path.
description.fs-rename_file: Renames or moves a file, replacing the destination file if needed.
description.fs-write_binary_file: Writes binary data provided as a hexadecimal string to a file, or appends it to an existing one.
description.fs-write_file: Writes text content to a file, creating missing directories as needed.
description.lua-execute: Runs a Lua script with access to the application's built-in API and returns the result along with printed messages.
description.lua-get_script_info: Shows detailed information about a registered Lua script, including its full content.
description.lua-list_scripts: Lists all registered Lua scripts with their namespaces, paths, and documentation.
description.lua-move_script: Moves or renames a registered Lua script from one path to another.
description.lua-register_or_update_script: Registers a new Lua script or updates an existing one, making it available in the Lua environment under a given namespace.
description.lua-remove_script: Removes a registered Lua script by its relative path.
description.math-calculate: Evaluates a mathematical expression, supporting constants, functions, integrals, derivatives, and complex numbers.
description.math-solve: Finds real roots of an equation numerically within a specified search range.
description.math-solve_complex: Finds complex roots of an equation numerically across a region of the complex plane.
description.memory-append_log: Adds a new event entry to the event log of the specified memory block.
description.memory-clear: Clears stored facts and/or event logs from a memory block while keeping the block itself intact.
description.memory-delete_log: Permanently removes an event log entry from a memory block by its ID.
description.memory-forget_fact: Deletes a fact from a memory block by its ID; by default keeps it restorable later.
description.memory-retrieve_fact: Finds facts in memory blocks matching the query and returns them with their IDs.
description.memory-search_log: Searches the event logs of memory blocks for entries matching a text query.
description.memory-store_fact: Stores a fact in a memory block with a given importance rating.
description.memory-view_logs: Shows event log entries from memory blocks, newest first, with optional time filtering.
description.metatools-create_or_update: Creates a new custom tool or updates an existing one, defining its name, description, parameters, and execution script.
description.metatools-delete: Deletes an existing custom tool.
description.metatools-get_info: Returns full details about a custom tool: description, parameters, execution script, and other settings.
description.metatools-list: Lists all existing custom tools with their names and titles.
description.metatools-rename: Renames an existing custom tool to a new name.
description.python-get_installed_packages_list: Lists the packages installed in the current Python virtual environment.
description.random-GUID: Generates a new globally unique identifier (GUID) that can be used to label or identify objects.
description.random-check_chance: Checks whether a given probability (as a percentage) comes true and returns success or failure.
description.random-coin_flip: Simulates a coin toss and returns either 'Heads' or 'Tails'.
description.random-dice_roll: Rolls one or more dice with a chosen number of sides and returns each result and the total.
description.random-float: Generates a random fractional number between the specified minimum and maximum values.
description.random-integer: Generates a random whole number between the specified minimum and maximum values, inclusive.
description.random-items_from_list: Picks the requested number of random items from a given list.
description.random-shuffle_list: Returns the items of a given list rearranged in a random order.
description.shell-bash: Runs a Bash command or script from the current working directory, with optional live terminal output.
description.shell-batch: Runs a Windows batch command or script from the current working directory, with optional live terminal output.
description.shell-powershell: Runs a PowerShell command or script from the current working directory, with optional live terminal output.
description.skill-load: Loads a skill by its name and returns its contents.
description.time-get: Returns the current time, either in the user's timezone or in a specified timezone.
description.time-wait: Pauses for a given duration (hours, minutes, seconds) and shows live progress while waiting.
description.wd-list: Lists all working directories configured for the current chat session.
description.wd-switch: Switches the active working directory for the current chat session.
description.web-download: Downloads a file from a URL and saves it to the working directory.
description.web-fetch: Loads a web page by URL and returns its content as markdown, HTML, or sanitized text.
description.web-parse: Fetches an HTML page, selects elements by a CSS selector, and returns their text content.
description.web-request: Sends an HTTP request (GET, POST, PUT, or DELETE) to a URL and returns the response status, headers, and body content.
description.web-search: Searches the web through multiple search engines and returns results with titles, links, descriptions, and extra metadata.
description.web-search_get_engines: Lists available search engines with their supported categories and capabilities.
description.web-status: Checks whether a website is reachable and reports its HTTP status code, response time, and server details.

// Tool categories
category.agents: Agents
category.database: Database
category.filesystem: File system
category.forms: Forms
category.general: General
category.mathematics: Mathematics
category.memory: Memory
category.metatools: Meta-tools
category.random: Random
category.scripting: Scripting
category.skills: Skills
category.time: Time
category.web: Web
category.workdir: Working directories

// Tool statuses, behaviours, call actions, sources, fixed flags.
arguments: Tool arguments:
behaviour.accessoutsideworkdir: Access outside working directory
behaviour.accessoutsideworkdir_hint: The tool accesses locations outside the configured working directory.
behaviour.adhoc: Ad-hoc (special tools)
behaviour.adhoc_hint: Special tools created for disposable execution (scripted tools, for example)
behaviour.agentexecution: Agent execution
behaviour.agentexecution_hint: The tool invokes, manages, or coordinates other AI agents.
behaviour.clipboardaccess: Clipboard access
behaviour.clipboardaccess_hint: The tool accesses the clipboard for reading or writing text data.
behaviour.clipboardread: Clipboard read
behaviour.clipboardread_hint: The tool reads text data from the clipboard.
behaviour.clipboardwrite: Clipboard write
behaviour.clipboardwrite_hint: The tool writes text data to the clipboard.
behaviour.databasechange: Database change
behaviour.databasechange_hint: The tool changes data or schema in a connected database.
behaviour.databasecustomconnect: Custom database connection
behaviour.databasecustomconnect_hint: The tool connects to a database using a custom connection string.
behaviour.databaseread: Database read
behaviour.databaseread_hint: The tool reads data from a connected database.
behaviour.directorydelete: Delete directories
behaviour.directorydelete_hint: The tool removes entire directory trees including their contents.
behaviour.directoryedit: Edit directories (move, rename, copy)
behaviour.directoryedit_hint: The tool modifies the directory structure (move, rename, copy).
behaviour.directoryread: Read directories
behaviour.directoryread_hint: The tool enumerates or lists the contents of directories.
behaviour.executeexternalprocess: Execute external process
behaviour.executeexternalprocess_hint: The tool spawns or executes an external operating system process.
behaviour.filedelete: Delete files
behaviour.filedelete_hint: The tool permanently removes files from the filesystem.
behaviour.filedirectorycreate: Create files and directories
behaviour.filedirectorycreate_hint: The tool creates new files or directories on the filesystem.
behaviour.fileedit: Edit files
behaviour.fileedit_hint: The tool modifies existing file content or metadata without deleting it.
behaviour.fileread: Read files
behaviour.fileread_hint: The tool reads the contents of files.
behaviour.internetaccess: Internet access
behaviour.internetaccess_hint: The tool performs network requests to external services or APIs.
behaviour.longrunningtask: Long-running task
behaviour.longrunningtask_hint: The tool may run for an extended period due to heavy computation or network latency.
behaviour.mcp: MCP (external server)
behaviour.mcp_hint: The tool originates from an external MCP server and may have unpredictable behaviour.
behaviour.meta: Meta-tool (LLM-created)
behaviour.meta_hint: The tool is a meta-tool created at runtime by the LLM via Lua/Python scripting.
behaviour.none: Safe (no specific behaviour)
behaviour.none_hint: Purely computational or informational tasks (math, random, time).
behaviour.possiblyunexpected: Potentially unexpected actions
behaviour.possiblyunexpected_hint: The tool may perform unexpected or uncontrollable actions.
behaviour.readsecrets: Read secrets and sensitive data
behaviour.readsecrets_hint: The tool may expose sensitive information such as passwords, API keys or tokens.
behaviour.runterminal: Run in terminal
behaviour.runterminal_hint: The tool runs commands in an embedded terminal emulator with interactive I/O.
behaviour.scriptaccess: Tool and script access
behaviour.scriptaccess_hint: The tool creates, modifies, or deletes other tools and user scripts at runtime.
behaviour.semanticmemoryclear: Semantic memory clear
behaviour.semanticmemoryclear_hint: The tool clears semantic memory blocks and may cause data loss.
behaviour.semanticmemorydelete: Semantic memory delete entry
behaviour.semanticmemorydelete_hint: Tool removes facts and logs from semantic memory.
behaviour.semanticmemoryread: Semantic memory read
behaviour.semanticmemoryread_hint: Tool can read facts and logs from semantic memory.
behaviour.semanticmemorywrite: Semantic memory write
behaviour.semanticmemorywrite_hint: Tool can write facts and logs to semantic memory.
behaviour.userinteraction: User interaction (forms, confirmations)
behaviour.userinteraction_hint: The tool requires user input via forms, confirmations, file pickers, etc.
behaviour.workdirchange: Change working directory
behaviour.workdirchange_hint: The tool switches the active working directory, affecting the base for all relative file operations.
call.action.approve_with_notes: Approve with notes
call.action.approve_with_wait.hint: Approve and ask agent to wait
call.action.cancel: Cancel tool
call.action.cancel_with_reason: Cancel with reason
call.action.cancel_with_wait.hint: Cancel and ask agent to wait
call.action.commit_notes: Submit
call.notes.placeholder: Enter note/reason...
call.status.cancelled: Cancelled
call.status.confirming: Confirmation needed
call.status.executing: Executing...
call.status.failed: Failed
call.status.pending: Pending
call.status.pre_executing: Analyzing...
call.status.success: Success
call.status.unknown: Unknown
copy_arguments: Copy arguments
copy_result: Copy result
fixed: Fixed tool
fixed.hint: This tool is always enabled while its context is present and cannot be disabled.
